From ae78c89e3808843cd73dcd9eaf42c53652f019dd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian MacDonald <ian@netstatz.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 15:00:34 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 066/104] fix(models): serialize writes to repository
 provenance files

Pulls of different models hold different repository locks but can record
into the same shared auxiliary repository. Each write loads the file,
changes it and saves it through one fixed .tmp name. Two pulls could
interleave, and one would then drop the other's entry and pin. A single
process-wide lock now covers the read-modify-write in
record_processed_model and in forget_registry_provenance. Nothing else
is locked while it is held, so it cannot deadlock. Because writers no
longer overlap, the shared .tmp name is now safe.

Assisted-by: claude:opus-5.5
